# US English letter-to-sound.
#
# One block a letter and its arms in order, the first that matches winning.
# The last arm of a block is the bare letter: what it says when nothing else
# applies. `says nothing' swallows the letters and lays no phones down.
#
# The letters are the language's own characters and the phones are the ETI
# phone letters, the same ones enus.dict uses. tools/rules/letters.py writes
# rules/et_phone.up out of this, and test/words.sh says whether any of 24,318
# words moved.

letter b
  bt   says t     # debt
  b    says b
